<title>FINLAND: NOKIA WINS $30 MLN ORDER FROM THAI TAC.</title>
<headline>NOKIA WINS $30 MLN ORDER FROM THAI TAC.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy said on Wednesday it won an order worth over $30 million to deliver synchronised digital hierarchy (SDH) fibre optic transmission solutions to Total Access Communications (TAC), part of the UCOM group of Thailand.  </p>
<p>The equipment would be delivered for the third phase of TAC's mobile network, extending its services to include corporate communications services, Nokia said.</p>
<p>&quot;With the Nokia SYNFONET product family operators who face sporadic and unpredictable network growth are assured of being able to build their network as they grow,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
